## Evidence and next phase

Public smoke passed. The candidate suite covers native equivalence (including
witness stripping/digest order, empty input, malformed input, and native byte
limits), validation, pipelining, cancellation/event order, eight concurrent
clients, disconnects, writer lock, schema rejection, seeded recovery, process
crashes, durable cancellation, count backpressure, large/fragmented lines, and a
nonreading peer. Independent inspection happens only after the writer stops.

ReleaseSafe checks and external process-crash tests do not establish exhaustive
race freedom or power-loss durability. Native allocation and actual storage I/O
failures were reviewed in code but not fault-injected. Four native worker slots
exist by construction; externally held native-entry concurrency qualification
remains unclaimed. Byte-accounting invariants are checked, but simultaneous
64 MiB admission saturation was not forced by a timing hook. No performance
comparison or optimization conclusion is claimed.

For maintenance, preserve schema 1 and receipt identity. The relevant native call
is in `Pool.worker`; scheduling and journal policy remain in the coordinator.
Do not activate ABI v2 until the next phase explicitly requires it.
